WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.203 --> 00:00:01.867
Ladies and gentlemen, it's hard to believe

2
00:00:01.867 --> 00:00:03.968
25 years ago this week

3
00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:06.878
my first guest was elected the 42nd president

4
00:00:06.878 --> 00:00:08.456
of the United States,

5
00:00:08.456 --> 00:00:11.288
which led to the longest period of peace time expansion

6
00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:12.752
in American history.

7
00:00:12.752 --> 00:00:14.702
We are honored

8
00:00:14.702 --> 00:00:17.969
to have him join us here in Harlem tonight.

9
00:00:17.969 --> 00:00:20.821
Please welcome, President Bill Clinton!

10
00:00:20.821 --> 00:00:23.821
(audience cheering)

11
00:00:23.821 --> 00:00:26.321
(jazzy music)

12
00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:51.803
Whoa.

13
00:00:52.967 --> 00:00:56.550
(audience cheering loudly)

14
00:00:57.623 --> 00:00:58.456
So...

15
00:01:02.178 --> 00:01:03.532
You were great at Sylvia's.

16
00:01:03.532 --> 00:01:06.047
You think I have a future at Sylvia's,

17
00:01:06.047 --> 00:01:06.880
is that what you're saying?

18
00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:07.905
I do.

19
00:01:07.905 --> 00:01:09.522
But I have one question.

20
00:01:09.522 --> 00:01:11.700
Did they let you keep the hairnet?

21
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.868
(Conan laughing)

22
00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:14.975
That's not a good look for me.

23
00:01:14.975 --> 00:01:16.290
It's really not a good look for me.

24
00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:17.525
It was so cool.

25
00:01:17.525 --> 00:01:18.912
Look, it's a great place.

26
00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.366
[Conan] Yes, you've been there?

27
00:01:20.366 --> 00:01:21.246
You've eaten there quite--

28
00:01:21.246 --> 00:01:22.079
Oh yes.

29
00:01:22.079 --> 00:01:22.912
many times.
It's great.

30
00:01:22.912 --> 00:01:23.745
Yeah.

31
00:01:23.745 --> 00:01:25.008
And they're great people.

32
00:01:25.008 --> 00:01:25.841
Yep.

33
00:01:25.841 --> 00:01:28.735
And it's part of what makes Harlem special.

34
00:01:28.735 --> 00:01:31.079
My office is two blocks from here.

35
00:01:31.079 --> 00:01:31.920
[Conan] Yeah, yeah.

36
00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:32.753
It's great.

37
00:01:32.753 --> 00:01:34.003
It's amazing.

38
00:01:35.245 --> 00:01:38.787
I couldn't believe in the introduction,

39
00:01:38.787 --> 00:01:40.737
you were elected president,

40
00:01:40.737 --> 00:01:42.194
time does strange things,

41
00:01:42.194 --> 00:01:44.880
25 years ago this week.

42
00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.386
25 years ago this week.

43
00:01:46.386 --> 00:01:48.368
And the first question I had was,

44
00:01:48.368 --> 00:01:51.593
what was the hardest thing to get used to

45
00:01:51.593 --> 00:01:54.301
on the first day that you were no longer president,

46
00:01:54.301 --> 00:01:57.137
as a civilian, 'cause that's gotta be a massive change.

47
00:01:57.137 --> 00:01:59.934
What was the hardest thing to get used to?

48
00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:02.615
They don't play a song when you walk in the room anymore.

49
00:02:02.615 --> 00:02:05.497
(audience laughing)

50
00:02:05.497 --> 00:02:07.422
I mean, it's amazing.

51
00:02:07.422 --> 00:02:10.210
(Conan laughing)

52
00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:12.654
For three or four weeks, I was totally lost.

53
00:02:12.654 --> 00:02:14.024
I didn't know where I was.

54
00:02:14.024 --> 00:02:17.033
I was, "Where is Hail to the Chief?"

55
00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:18.081
I kept thinking--

56
00:02:18.081 --> 00:02:20.577
You could probably work it out so they play it for you.

57
00:02:20.577 --> 00:02:22.356
You get a little boombox and just push a button

58
00:02:22.356 --> 00:02:24.356
when you come into a room.

59
00:02:24.356 --> 00:02:26.411
Yeah, but then, if you think you're still there,

60
00:02:26.411 --> 00:02:28.120
that's a really dangerous thing.

61
00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.870
(Conan laughing)

